==Strategy==
Starters can easily beat the first stage and ignore the rest as the first stage is guaranteed to drop the [[True Form]] of [[Li'l Madoka (Rare Cat)|Li'l Madoka]].

For those players who want to clear this entire gauntlet, using [[:Category:Witch Killer Cats|Witch Killer Cats]] would be mandatory past the first stage, as Walpurgisnacht's extreme stats begin to skyrocket immediately. It is also recommended to bring [[Li'l Madoka (Rare Cat)|Li'l Madoka]] and [[Li'l Homura (Special Cat)|Li'l Homura]] for the [[My Very Best Friend (Combo)|My Very Best Friend]] Combo. This single Combo could be the difference between victory and defeat, as it dramatically boosts effectiveness of the Witch Killer ability. In other words, wait for the [[Guaranteed Uber Rare Cat Campaign|guaranteed Uber]] event at the end of the collab and use whatever you get to beat this gauntlet (if you don't have them already), or be ready to waste hours on each of the last few stages, where this enemy can have up to 14.4 million health, making it impenetrable without these specialists.

Of the Collab Ubers, here are how all of them do on this stage.

* [[Sayaka Miki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sayaka Miki]] - Highest health and DPS among all Ubers. Also only has 2 knockbacks, the least out of all the Ubers, so she won't have to walk up as often. She also gets even stronger after Strengthen activates. Without a doubt the best for this stage.
* [[Homura Akemi (Uber Rare Cat)|Homura Akemi]] - Has less stats and more knockbacks than Sayaka, but compensates with slow immune, which means she can immediately continue fighting without delays.
* [[Kyoko Sakura (Uber Rare Cat)|Kyoko Sakura]] - Tougher than Homura, but unfortunately not immune to slow.
* [[Madoka Kaname (Uber Rare Cat)|Madoka Kaname]] - Fast and has high range. Only issue is the DPS.
* [[Mami Tomoe (Uber Rare Cat)|Mami Tomoe]] - Works very much like Madoka, except more damage in exchange for less speed and range.
* [[Bebe (Uber Rare Cat)|Nagisa]] - Not the best uber for the stage as she cannot withstand Walpurgisnacht at all.
* [[Madoka Cat & Homura (Uber Rare Cat)|Madoka Cat & Homura]] - Does not have Witch Killer and thus should not be used here.

As for units outside of this collab, only a few of them would be particularly useful. [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] has the speed and recharge to get in Walpurgisnacht's range and trigger her attack without letting her advance, making it particularly useful at keeping Walpurgisnacht from reaching and one-shotting the base. While not required, boosting it to level 45 or above helps immensely, as this level ensures that it can live a single hit from Walpurgisnacht (up to 480k damage per hit) without Defense combos. Stone Cat could be used to solo Walpurgisnacht, though this would take a massive, unreasonable amount of time since Stone does minuscule damage. Instead, it should mainly be used to support other units such as the aforementioned Witch Killers. Alternatively, [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] with the talents Resist Slow and Speed Up, as well as some extra help from speed combos or the Sniper the Cat item, can also permanently stall the enemy. This allows you to cover the downtime of your Witch Killer Ubers.

Other rushers, such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], among others, can help whittle Walpurgisnacht's health with their high speed, though they should not be used alone. Additionally, timing these fast units becomes easier with the help of Speed combos, and Attack combos help them whittle Walpurgisnacht's health down faster.

